%SIXMD 1
# @?DTFSPROBE - IDENTIFY A DECTAPE FILESYSTEM

## @?OPTIONS

NONE.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?/DEV/DTC0
DECTAPE DEVICE TO PROBE.  THE CURRENT RESIDENT HELPER ACCEPTS DTC0.

### @?[DEEP]
OPTIONAL DEEP VALIDATION.  FOR TENEX MEDIA THIS ALSO VALIDATES FILE BLOCK
CHAINS RATHER THAN ONLY DIRECTORY AND OWNER-TABLE SHAPE.

## DESCRIPTION

DTFSPROBE IS THE SHORT-LIVED USERSPACE MEDIA-PERSONALITY PROBE USED BY THE
DTFS MOUNT AND CHECK PATHS.  IT IDENTIFIES NATIVE, TENEX, OR ITS DECTAPE
LAYOUT WITHOUT KEEPING THE DIRECTORY-SCAN WORKSPACE RESIDENT IN THE SHELL OR
KERNEL.

ON SUCCESS THE PROCESS EXIT STATUS IS THE INTERNAL DTFS PERSONALITY VALUE.
THE COMMAND IS PRIMARILY AN IMPLEMENTATION HELPER; NORMAL ADMINISTRATION USES
MOUNT.DTFS OR FSCK.DTFS.

## @?FILES

### @?/DEV/DTC0
CURRENT DECTAPE DEVICE PROBED BY THE HELPER.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?1 - INVALID INVOCATION OR MEDIA COULD NOT BE IDENTIFIED
### @?OTHER - IDENTIFIED DTFS PERSONALITY VALUE

## @?SEE ALSO

### @?FSCK.DTFS
### @?MOUNT.DTFS
